Don't know of any SDK interface; there's an SDL interface which is
normally built under UNIX but might work under MS-Windows - I've never
tried or there's Clive Crous's noeGNUd interface which can also use SDL.

In any event, Slash'EM has changed how you eat of the floor in the core
game so the effect you are seeing may have nothing to do with the interface.
There is a new modifier "," which means objects in this place. Thus to
eat a corpse without picking it up you say "e," and similarly to drink
potions, etc. This makes life much easier when there are many corpses in
a pile since you don't have to skip through a long list of "There is a
<corpse> here, eat it?" every time you want to eat something from your
inventory.

